==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{Ger.|ang}} ''*haira-'', from {{IE.|ang}} ''*kei-, *koi-''. Cognate with Old Saxon ''[[her|hēr]]'', Old High German ''[[her|hēr]]'' (German ''[[hehr]]'' ‘august, holy’), Old Norse ''[[hárr]]'' ‘grey’.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/ha:ɹ/}}

===Adjective===
'''hār'''

# Grey-haired, [[old]] and [[grey]], [[venerable]].

